.SS "bool stumpless_close_sqlite3_target_and_db (const struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * target)"

.PP
Closes a SQLite3 target and its database handle\&. This function can fail if the database handle cannot be closed\&. In this case, the target is not closed, and no resources are released\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Unsafe\fP This function is not thread safe as it destroys resources that other threads would use if they tried to reference this target\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the destruction of a lock that may be in use as well as the use of the memory deallocation function to release memory\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed, and the memory deallocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.2\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The SQLite3 target to close\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if the target was closed, and false if not\&. An error code is set appropriately if the target could not be closed\&. 
.RE
.PP

