.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_open_sqlite3_target (const char * name)"

.PP
Opens a SQLite3 target\&. This is equivalent to calling \fBstumpless_open_sqlite3_target_with_options\fP with SQLITE_OPEN_READWRITE | SQLITE_OPEN_CREATE as the flags and NULL as the VFS module name\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name is not modified by any other threads during execution\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of memory allocation functions\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the memory allocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.2\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP The name of the database to open\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The opened target if no error is encountered\&. In the event of an error, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_open_sqlite3_target_from_db (void * db)"

.PP
Opens a SQLite3 target with an already-open database handle\&. This function allows a specialized database to be opened, or an existing handle to be used\&. For example, if an in-memory database is needed, it can be opened and then passed to this function for logging\&.
.PP
Note that there are two close functions for SQLite3 targets: \fBstumpless_close_sqlite3_target_and_db\fP and \fBstumpless_close_sqlite3_target_only\fP\&. Be sure to call the appropriate one depending on whether you want this handle to be closed when the target is closed\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of memory allocation functions\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the memory allocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.2\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdb\fP The database handle to use\&. This should be a sqlite3 *, though it is not declared as such so that sqlite3 headers are not required\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The opened target if no error is encountered\&. In the event of an error, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_open_sqlite3_target_with_options (const char * name, int flags, const char * vfs)"

.PP
Opens a SQLite3 target with the provided options\&. The three parameters are passed directly to sqlite3_open_v2\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name race:vfs\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name and vfs are not modified by any other threads during execution\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of memory allocation functions\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the memory allocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.2\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP The name of the database to open\&.
.br
\fIflags\fP Flags as defined for sqlite3_open_v2\&.
.br
\fIvfs\fP The name of the VFS module to use as defined by sqlite3_open_v2\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
