.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_set_sqlite3_insert_sql (struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * target, const char * sql)"

.PP
Sets the SQL statement used to insert entries into the database\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe as a mutex is used to coordinate the changes with other target modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP Thisi function is not signal safe, as a non-reentrant lock is used to coordinate the read of the target with other potential accesses\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock used for the target may not be completed\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.2\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The target to set the insert SQL for\&.
.br
\fIsql\fP The new SQL insertion statement to use for the target\&. This string must be valid for the duration of its use in the target, as a pointer to it is kept internally\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The modified target on success, or NULL on failure\&. In the event of failure an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_set_sqlite3_prepare (struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * target, \fBstumpless_sqlite3_prepare_func_t\fP preparer, void * data)"

.PP
Set the function used to prepare statements for entries to this target\&. Preparation functions take three arguments: the entry that is being sent to the database target, a pointer provided when the function is set, and an output parameter where the number of prepared statements to use is written\&. The function should return a pointer to an array of prepared statements that should be committed to the database for the entry, or NULL if an error occurs\&. The default prepare function is \fBstumpless_sqlite3_prepare\fP, which is a good place to look for an example\&.
.PP
Note that the return type is a void * instead of the actual type of sqlite3_stmt **\&. This is so that the SQLite3 headers are not needed\&.
.PP
Be careful when using a custom prepare function in builds where SQLite was directly embedded into Stumpless instead of dynamically linked\&. If this is the case, using a single databse handle in both SQLite functions compiled into Stumpless and SQLite functions compiled in a separate module may cause serious issues, for example due to static data structures\&. The example \fBsqlite3_example\&.c\fP does this, and is a good way to check if you are in this situation as it will fail in this scenario\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe as a mutex is used to coordinate accesses of the target structures\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP Thisi function is not signal safe, as a non-reentrant lock is used to coordinate the read of the target with other potential accesses\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock used for the target may not be completed\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.2\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The target to set the function for\&.
.br
\fIpreparer\fP The new prepare function to use in the target\&.
.br
\fIdata\fP A pointer that will be passed to the prepare function on each invocation\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The modified target on success, or NULL on failure\&. In the event of failure an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void * stumpless_sqlite3_prepare (const struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry, void * data, size_t * count)"

.PP
The default prepare function used for SQLite3 targets\&. This function will generate a single prepared statement based on the target's current insert SQL statement\&. See \fBstumpless_set_sqlite3_insert_sql\fP for how to set the SQL used by this function\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe as a mutex is used to coordinate accesses of the entry and target structures\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP Thisi function is not signal safe, as a non-reentrant lock is used to coordinate the read of the target with other potential accesses\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock used for the target may not be completed\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.2\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIentry\fP The entry to prepare the statement based on\&.
.br
\fIdata\fP The internal SQLite3 target structure\&.
.br
\fIcount\fP A pointer to an output variable where the number of valid prepared statements will be written to\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A pointer to an array of sqlite3_stmt pointers on success, or NULL on failure\&. In the event of failure an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

